{"verdict":"changes_requested","issues":[{"severity":"major","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":57,"description":"The prescribed minimal fix has been correctly applied — the live_preview configuration block is present in the options object with management_token, enable, and host fields, and the corresponding env vars (CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN, CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_ENABLE, CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST) are destructured at lines 17-24. This matches the root cause analysis exactly. However, no vitest unit tests were added to verify the live_preview configuration is present in the exported options object, that enable defaults to false when CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_ENABLE is not 'true', or that the host defaults to empty string. Per review criteria, new features must have corresponding vitest unit tests in test/unit/ mirroring the src/ path. Grep across test/ for live_preview, livePreview, ContentstackContext, ContentstackProvider returned zero results.","suggestedFix":"Add a vitest unit test at test/unit/services/contentstack.test.ts that imports the options object and asserts: (1) options.live_preview is defined, (2) options.live_preview.management_token equals CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN, (3) options.live_preview.enable is false when CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_ENABLE is unset or not 'true', (4) options.live_preview.host defaults to empty string when CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST is unset. Mock process.env as needed."}],"summary":"The prescribed minimal fix for AMSD-2041 has been correctly and concisely applied: the live_preview configuration block (management_token, enable, host) was added to the options object in src/services/contentstack.ts, and the three corresponding env vars were destructured from process.env. This matches the root cause analysis exactly — no over-engineering, no unnecessary new code paths. The Contentstack SDK's Stack initializer will now fetch draft/unpublished content when preview mode is active (enable=true) and serve published content when it is not (enable=false), satisfying all seven verification criteria through the SDK's built-in live preview functionality. The only gap is the absence of vitest unit tests for this configuration change, which is required by the review criteria for new features."}
